        "x1": 0.8904825870646766,
        "y1": 0.8691760299625468
      },
      "text": "Variable -1 (SE) 95% CI P Value % time in clinic 1.1* (.19) 8.4 (1.2) 11 (.96) 0.7-1.4 5.2-9.5 Reference 6.5 .01 .01 Reference Reference Academic year 1982 ~14 (4.0) <.01 1983 20.3 (3.8) 1983 22 (4) <01 1984 ~18 (3.7) ~26 to .01 1985 18 (3.7) =23.8 to -9.6 .01 1987 19.2 (3.5) ~26.2 to -12.3 1988 24 (4) 31 to   16 <.01 1989 27 (4.3) 01 1990 4.5 (2.6) ~9.7 to 0.7 .09 1991 8.9 (2.4) 1992 <01 1993 ~11 (21) .01 1994 13.2 (2.2) <.01 1995 218.8 to -10.5 1996 <.01 1998 6.0 (21) ~10 to =1.9 1998 Reference Reference Reference",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4986185737976782,
        "y0": 0.8730749063670412,
        "x1": 0.8910995024875621,
        "y1": 0.8955468164794007
      },
      "text": "All visits (sick and WCC visits) were included. Intercept   47. CI indicates confidence interval. * value of 1.1 is for a change of 1% of time in continuity clinic.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4986185737976782,
        "y0": 0.8955468164794007,
        "x1": 0.889995024875622,
        "y1": 0.9305031210986268
      },
      "text": "The effect size of a increase in 1 half day (10% of resident’s time) is 11% increase in continuity.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    }
